\p
\v 1 \add Back\add* in the time¦123781 when the tribal¦123783 leaders¦123783 ruled \add Yisrael (Israel)\add*, there was \add a drought which caused\add* a shortage of food¦123790, so a man¦123788 from \add the town of\add* Beyt¦123789-Lehem \add !(Bethlehem¦123789)\add* in the Yehudah¦123791 \add !(Judah¦123791) region¦123793\add* went¦123787 to¦123792 live in the country¦123793 of Moab¦123794 \add for a while\add*, taking his wife¦123796 and¦123780 their two¦123797 sons¦123798.
\v 2 The man's¦123801 name was Elimelek¦123802 and he was married to Naomi¦123805, and their sons' names were Mahlon¦123811 and Kilion¦123812. (They were part of \add the clan of\add* Efratah¦123813 from¦123814 Beyt¦123814-Lehem in Yehudah¦123816.) They travelled to the Moab¦123820 countryside and lived there¦123823.
\v 3 Then¦123825 Naomi's¦123828 husband¦123827 Elimelek¦123826 died¦123825, and¦123825 she¦123830 was¦123829 left¦123829 with her¦123832 two¦123831 sons¦123832.
