\v 5 Mahlon¦123853 and Kilion¦123854 both¦123857 also died¦123849, and Naomi was¦123855 left¦123855 without¦123857 her husband¦123859 or her two¦123857 sons¦123858.
\s1 Ruth accompanies Naomi back to Beyt-Lehem
\rem /s1 Naomi and Ruth Return to Bethlehem; Naomi and Ruth Return; Naomi and Her Moabite Daughters-in-Law
\p
\v 6 \add One day\add* Naomi was in the¦123865 countryside there in Moab¦123866 when she heard¦123868 someone telling about¦123863 how Yahweh¦123874 had helped his people¦123877 in Yisrael and¦123861 that¦123871 now they had plenty of¦123877 food¦123880, so she got ready to return¦123864 \add to Beyt-Lehem\add* with¦123869 her¦123863 \add two\add* daughters-in-law¦123863.
\v 7 The three of them left¦123882 the place¦123885 where¦123886 they'd been¦123887 living \add in Moab\add* and¦123882 \add started walking\add* along the road back to Yehudah¦123899 \add !(Judah¦123899)\add*.
\v 8 Then¦123901 Naomi¦123902 said¦123901 to her¦123904 two¦123903 daughters-in-law¦123904, “Both of you should go¦123905 back to your parents' homes. \add I pray that\add* Yahweh¦123912 will treat you with the¦123919 same faithfulness¦123914 that you showed to your now-deceased husbands and¦123920 to me¦123920.
\v 9 May¦123922 Yahweh¦123923 enable \add both\add* of you¦123924 to¦123924 find new husbands¦123929 and find peace and happiness in your new homes with them.”
\p Then she¦123930 kissed¦123930 them as they all wept¦123934 aloud.
\v 10 But¦123936 they¦123936 both said¦123936, “No, we'll¦123942 \add go\add* with¦123941 you¦123941 as you return¦123942 to¦123943 your¦123943 relatives.”
\p
\v 11 But¦123945 Naomi¦123946 responded¦123945, “No, go¦123950 back¦123947 to your homes my daughters¦123948. Why would you¦123950 bother coming with¦123956 me¦123951? It's not like I could still¦123952 give birth to \add more\add* sons¦123955 to become your husbands¦123959.
\v 12 Go¦123961 on back¦123961, my daughters¦123962, because¦123964 I'm¦123965 too¦123965 old¦123965 to¦123967 remarry. Even if¦123968 I did hope¦123973 for¦123966 that and got married tonight and had \add some\add* sons¦123980,
\v 13 could you wait¦123984 for them to grow¦123987 up \add so you could be remarried\add*? No¦123994, my daughters¦123994, what's hard for me, even more¦124001 than¦124001 your hardships, is that Yahweh¦124008 is using his power against me.”
\p
\v 14 Then¦124010 they¦124010 wailed and cried again¦124013, and Orpah¦124015 kissed¦124014 her¦124016 mother-in-law¦124016 \add goodbye and left\add*, but¦124010 Ruth¦124017 \add stayed and\add* clung¦124018 to¦124019 Naomi.
\v 15 Naomi said¦124021, “Look, your sister-in-law is going¦124031 back to her parents and¦124021 to her religion. Go¦124031 back with her.”
